*PPD-Adobe: "4.3"
*% SYNTHETIC FIXTURE - hand-written for testing ppdprobe.py.
*% Not derived from any vendor PPD. Models a driver that provides NO identity
*% escape: every ICC entry is a paper profile, the default is a real profile,
*% and no APCustomColorMatchingProfile choices are declared - only a forced
*% sRGB default.
*FormatVersion: "4.3"
*ModelName: "Example Inkjet No Escape"
*NickName: "Example Inkjet No Escape"
*ColorDevice: True
*cupsFilter: "application/vnd.cups-raster 0 /path/to/vendor/filter"

*OpenUI *YYIntent/Rendering Intent: PickOne
*DefaultYYIntent: 5
*YYIntent 5/Perceptual (Photo): ""
*YYIntent 1001/No Color Correction: ""
*CloseUI: *YYIntent

*OpenUI *ColorModel/Color Model: PickOne
*DefaultColorModel: RGB16
*ColorModel RGB16/RGB 16-bit: "<</cupsColorSpace 1/cupsBitsPerColor 16>>setpagedevice"
*CloseUI: *ColorModel

*cupsICCQualifier2: YYProfileID
*OpenUI *YYProfileID/ProfileID: PickOne
*DefaultYYProfileID: 1
*YYProfileID 1/Example_Generic.icc: ""
*YYProfileID 2/Example_Glossy.icc: ""
*YYProfileID 3/Example_Matte.icc: ""
*CloseUI: *YYProfileID

*cupsICCProfile RGB16.1./Example_Generic.icc: "/path/to/vendor/Example_Generic.icc"
*cupsICCProfile RGB16.2./Example_Glossy.icc: "/path/to/vendor/Example_Glossy.icc"
*cupsICCProfile RGB16.3./Example_Matte.icc: "/path/to/vendor/Example_Matte.icc"

*APSupportsCustomColorMatching: True
*APDefaultCustomColorMatchingProfile: sRGB
